      "documentConcept": "Salesforce CDC versus custom Platform Events for Case alerting",
      "canonicalConceptId": "concept:9042520b5aaf02f8b404f898750b10b17b67cd1feaebd51dfd018d878ecff75d",
      "text": "CDC automatically reports record changes on enabled objects. Custom Platform Events carry a producer-defined business signal and payload. For Case alerting, CDC avoids custom publishing coverage, while custom events allow a deliberate alert contract. Filtered CDC channels can reduce delivery volume, so selectivity alone does not mandate custom events. Both event types use Pub/Sub API and share the delivery allocation. Custom-event publish timing must match the consumer\u2019s need for committed data. CDC is asynchronous and is not an absolute no-loss guarantee. These are design implications of the documented event models; this probe does not prescribe Case transition rules.",
